<blockquote class="uncited"><div>I already told you that's the same procedure for all the STM32 based transceiver.<br>You have never read someone bricked their device flashing the OpenGD77 firmware, that never happen. The only thing that could happen is a wrong firmware get flashed and the device stays in bootloader mode, waiting for a correct firmware to be flashed. That's all.<br><br>The MD-9600/MD-UV3x0/RT-3S/DM-1701 are working the same, in firmware flashing point of view. Only the USB cable differs.<br><br>You have tons of video on YT about this topic. Don't expect me to take you by the hand to flash the firmware, there are enough Howtos and threads here, YT videos, etc, about this topic.<br><br>Sorry to be a bit harsh, but since you're an Ham Radio, it means you're a bit technical person, used to document yourself.<br><br>Thanks.</div></blockquote>In law school, I took the course, Secured Transactions, from a renowned genius in his field, Professor Stefan Riesenfeld.<br><br>He was so brilliant that when someone would ask him a question, he would respond in his German accent: "Why would you ask that question?  You STUPID DUMMKOPF!!!<br><br>That's all I have to say about your style of responding to my questions, but thank you for pointing out that there is no fear of "bricking" any radio with OpenGD77.  With that self-confidence, I easily installed OpenGD77 on my Baofeng DM-1701.<br><br>Now that I have proven how easy it is to upgrade the least expensive DMR HT to OpenGD77, I am bored with it and will offer it for sale at my cost to our local DMR Net next Monday night and go back to using my RD-5R and DM-5R!  Thank you!<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=1890">W7ML</a> — Thu Feb 13, 2025 5:42 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
