<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div><br>From the post:<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Note. We use the MD9600 firmware as the ‘donor’ firmware, because the CPU in the MD-UV380 is the same as in the MD9600, and the codec in the MD9600 firmware is identical to the MD-UV380 codec, and to use the MD-UV380 official firmware as the ‘donor’ would require a lot of additional work for the developers.</div></blockquote>The MD9600 original firmware is used as a donor file for the codec, it's not meant to be flashed at all. This is the case for all the STM32 based transceivers supported by the firmware.</div></blockquote>Yes, thank you. I did read all of that but it is above my pay grade. <br><br>I am an end-user, so reading the quote from the post still does not tell me if I must do this step; i.e., be a donor file for the DM-1701 as well.</div></blockquote>The thread title is: "<strong class="text-strong">TYT MD-UV380/390 / RT-3S / DM1701 Installation information</strong>", is that not clear enough ?  <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_biggrin.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":D" title="Very Happy"><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=56">F1RMB</a> — Sat Feb 08, 2025 7:02 am</p><hr />
